From 3f9c6b0d1e2a4c5d8f7e6a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xu Qianhui <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:31:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v2] drm/msm/dsi/phy: program PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES on the first PHY
 enable

dsi_7nm_phy_enable() pre-seeds pll_enable_cnt = 1 under pll_enable_lock
before anything else touches the PLL.  Every caller of
dsi_pll_enable_pll_bias() that runs on the bring-up path -
dsi_pll_7nm_vco_set_rate() (link clock set_rate) and
dsi_pll_7nm_vco_prepare() - then hits the early-return branch:

	if (pll->pll_enable_cnt++) {
		...
		return;
	}

so its PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES = 0xc0 write is skipped on the first (bonded)
bring-up and the register stays at 0x0.  Recalc/state save-restore paths
turn the bias on and off again around their register accesses, and
dsi_pll_disable_pll_bias() writes PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES back to 0 when the
counter drops to zero, so nothing else programs it either.

Panels wired for bonded DSI then come up with a blank display.  Write
PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES in dsi_7nm_phy_enable() as well; the write in
dsi_pll_enable_pll_bias() is kept for the paths that reach it with
pll_enable_cnt == 0.

Fixes: 44784327815b ("Revert "drm/msm: dsi: fix PLL init in bonded mode"")
Signed-off-by: Xu Qianhui <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
---
v2: the explanatory comment moved from the code into this commit message,
    as asked in <e4ul4zxjta4oyo5fpjjzwkykb4gicztcn7yrgjw7aer6bqowkw@6nx2arhvmyca>.
    The code now carries only the write plus a one-line reason.

 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
index 1fc3b4f0c0..b8d0b4c9a2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -1095,6 +1095,8 @@ static int dsi_7nm_phy_enable(struct msm_dsi_phy *phy,
 	data = DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0_DIGTOP_PWRDN_B |
 	       DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0_PLL_SHUTDOWNB;
 	writel(data, base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
+	/* dsi_pll_enable_pll_bias() is skipped after the pre-seed above. */
+	writel(0xc0, pll->phy->pll_base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pll->pll_enable_lock, flags);
 
 	/* Assert PLL core reset */
